## Test Categories

### Unit Tests
- Test individual functions and methods
- Mock external dependencies
- Focus on specific behavior
- Should be fast and isolated

### Integration Tests
- Test interactions between components
- Test real dependencies when possible
- Focus on data flow and interfaces
- May be slower than unit tests

### Thread Safety Tests
- Test concurrent access to shared resources
- Test race conditions and deadlocks
- Use multiple threads to stress test
- Verify thread-safe behavior

### Performance Tests
- Test performance characteristics
- Benchmark critical operations
- Detect performance regressions
- Set performance baselines

## Test Maintenance Best Practices

### Test Organization
- Group related tests in classes
- Use descriptive test names
- Add docstrings explaining test purpose
- Keep tests focused and single-purpose

### Test Data Management
- Use fixtures for common test data
- Create helper functions for test setup
- Use factories for complex object creation
- Keep test data minimal and relevant

### Test Documentation
- Document test purpose and scope
- Explain complex test scenarios
- Document test data requirements
- Keep documentation up-to-date

### Continuous Integration
- Run tests on every code change
- Maintain test coverage thresholds
- Monitor test execution time
- Alert on test failures

## Enforcement
Test maintenance is **MANDATORY** for all code changes. No code should be merged without corresponding test updates. Tests are the first line of defense against bugs and regressions.
